[statement]
A `!` entry is no need: a package whose name the request's package takes
is removed among the first removals where a kept package names that name
only in a `!` entry. `q` takes `y` from the installed `p`, and the kept
`k` states `!y<1`, which forbids neither, so apk removes `p` first, as
where nothing names `y`
(`a-package-losing-a-name-nothing-else-needs-is-removed-first`), not at
`q`'s turn, as where `k` depends on `y`
(`a-package-losing-a-name-it-provides-is-removed-at-the-turn-of-its-successor`).

[repository]
P:a
V:1

P:q
V:1
p:y=2

[installed]
P:p
V:1
p:y=1

P:k
V:1
D:!y<1

[world]
k

[request]
a
q

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove p 1
install a 1
install q 1
